    "cap_rate_used_pct": 6.5,
    "negative_leverage": true,
    "negative_leverage_note": "At a 6.50% going-in cap against an 8.71% debt constant, every dollar of acquisition debt costs more than the yield on the asset it buys. DSCR is scale-invariant here: NOI / debt service = (70% x 6.50%) / (60% x 8.71%) = 0.87x at any rent level. Two consequences follow and both matter for the decision: (1) a leveraged buyer cannot pay a 6.50% cap today, which thins the bid for the asset if it is sold; (2) the assumption set is internally consistent only for an unlevered or low-leverage buyer, so the model's sell-now price should be read as an unlevered-clearing number.",
